      "term": "Star stitch",
      "definition": "Pull up five loops (from the eye of the previous star, and from four consecutive stitches), then yarn over and draw through all six. Close with ch 1. The loops radiate out like a star."
    },
    {
      "slug": "turning-chain",
      "term": "Turning chain",
      "definition": "Two chains at the start of each star stitch row."
    },
