  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "star-stitch"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "star stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " baby blanket is 75 x 90 cm. Each star pulls five loops into a central point and closes them with one yarn-over, making a geometric star shape that tiles across the fabric. The reverse side is equally textured."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "DK cotton shows the star points cleanly. Each star occupies 2 stitches in width so the repeat is simple once the first row is established. Total yardage is around 370 g."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "DK cotton yarn",
              "qty": "370 g"
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "9 stars x 10 rows = 10 x 10 cm in DK cotton with a 4 mm hook. Work a test row of 18 stars and measure across."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "How to make a star"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "*Insert hook into the ch-1 eye of the previous star and pull up loop. Pull up loops from each of the next 4 stitches or chains (6 loops total on hook). Yarn over, pull through all 6 loops. Ch 1 to form the eye of the new star*. One star made."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Foundation chain"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chain 153 (76 star repeats x 2 ch + 1 starting chain)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "turning-chain"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "turning chain"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " of ch 2. Pull up a loop from 2nd and 3rd ch from hook, and from next 3 ch (5 loops + working loop). Yarn over, pull through all 6. Ch 1 (eye made). *Work star from eye + next 4 ch*. Repeat. Turn. (76 stars.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 2 and onward"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 2. Pull up loops from the ch-2 turning chain, the eye of the first star, and from the next 3 ch-1 eyes. Work star. Continue along row, each new star pulling from the previous eye and the next 4 stitches. Turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Repeat Row 2 until piece measures 90 cm. Fasten off."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Secure tails with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "weaving-in-ends"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "weaving in ends"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Block lightly to even the star points."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash 30 degrees gentle. Dry flat. The star structure holds well through washing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The shell stitch blanket uses a simpler fan motif in the same DK weight. Or try the bobble blanket for a raised texture that is easier to work at speed."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
